rong>, https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.23829</strong></p><p>DeepSeek-R1 and most=
 other reasoning models that followed focused on reward signals from easily=
 verifiable domains like code and math. This paper explores how to extend t=
hese methods to more complex areas like medicine, chemistry, psychology, ec=
onomics, and education, where answers are usually free-form and harder to v=
erify (beyond a simple correct/incorrect).</p><p>The authors find that usin=
g expert-written reference answers makes evaluation more feasible than expe=
cted, even in these broader domains. To provide reward signals, they introd=
uce a generative, soft-scoring method without needing heavy domain-specific=
 annotation.</p><div class=3D"captioned-image-container"><figure><a target=
